/-!
# Pullback of an affine chart along an arbitrary morphism of schemes

Let `(X, D, M)` be a triple as in Situation 0F8S, let `h : Y ⟶ X` be a morphism of schemes
along which the pullback `E = h⁻¹D` of the divisor is defined, let `(U, A, f, M^•)` be an affine
chart for `(X, D, M)` and let `V = Spec(B) ⊆ Y` be an affine open with `h(V) ⊆ U`.  Writing
`g ∈ B` for the image of `f`, this file proves the three assertions of Stacks tag 0F8T:

1. `(V, B, g, M^• ⊗_A B)` is an affine chart for `(Y, E, Lh^*M)`;
2. `I_i(M^•, f)B = I_i(M^• ⊗_A B, g)` in `B`;
3. if `(X, D, M)` is a good triple then so is `(Y, E, Lh^*M)`.

Assertion (2) is Stacks tag 0GSU, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.map_determinantalIdeal` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.BlowUpSquare.ChartBaseChange`; it is recorded here on
the chart produced by (1) as `pullback_determinantalIdeal`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.pullbackRingHom`: the map of
  coordinate rings `A = Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(Y, V) = B` induced by `h`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.pullbackRepresentsIso`: the
  isomorphism in `D(𝒪_V)` between the restriction to `V` of a complex representing `Lh^*M` and
  the sheaf of modules of `M^• ⊗_A B`.  This is the transport of the affine comparison square of
  Stacks 08DW part (2) to the two charts, and is the content of assertion (1).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.pullback`: **assertion (1)**, the
  chart `(V, B, g, M^• ⊗_A B)` for the pulled-back triple.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isRegular_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_ideal_eq_span`: a generator of
  the ideal of an effective Cartier divisor on an affine open is a nonzerodivisor.  This is what
  makes `g` a nonzerodivisor of `B`: it generates the ideal of `E = h⁻¹D` on `V`, and `h⁻¹D` is
  an effective Cartier divisor by hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.pullback_determinantalIdeal`:
  **assertion (2)** read on the pulled-back chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.isGoodTriple_pullback`: **assertion (3)**.

## How assertion (1) is proved

Three things have to be checked, and the source lists them in this order.

*`g` is a nonzerodivisor of `B`.*  By `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE` the ideal of
`E = h⁻¹D` on `V` is the extension of the ideal of `D` on `U`, hence `Ideal.span {g}`.  Since
`h⁻¹D` is an effective Cartier divisor, its stalk ideal at every point of `V` is generated by a
nonzerodivisor, so the germ of `g` is a nonzerodivisor in every stalk, and a section of the
structure sheaf whose germs are all nonzerodivisors is a nonzerodivisor.

*`g` cuts out `E ∩ V`.*  The same computation of `(D.comap h).ideal V`.

*`M^• ⊗_A B` represents `Lh^*M|_V`.*  This is `pullbackRepresentsIso`, and it is where the
affine comparison square enters.  The chain of isomorphisms in `D(𝒪_V)` is

* restriction along the open immersion `V ⟶ Y` is derived pullback along it
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.derivedRestrictIsoDerivedPullback`), so the restriction to
  `V` of `Lh^*M` is the derived pullback of `M|_U` along `h|_V : V ⟶ U`, by the composition
  formula of Stacks 0D5S applied to the square `V.ι ≫ h = h|_V ≫ U.ι`; this is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.openRestrictionDerivedPullbackIso`;
* `M|_U` is `M̃^•` transported along `U ≅ Spec A`, by the chart's `represents` field, after the
  object `M` has been carried from the situation's own model of the derived category to the
  standard one by `CategoryTheory.Localization.uniq`;
* the two triangles `h|_V ≫ (U ≅ Spec A)` and `(V ≅ Spec B) ≫ Spec (A ⟶ B)` are the same
  morphism `V ⟶ Spec A` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.toSpecΓ_SpecMap_appLE`), so the
  composition formula again replaces the derived pullback along `h|_V` by the derived pullback
  along `Spec (A ⟶ B)` followed by restriction along `V ≅ Spec B`;
* the derived pullback along `Spec (A ⟶ B)` of `M̃^•` is the degreewise pullback, because `M^•`
  is a bounded complex of finite free modules and therefore K-flat
  (`CochainComplex.KFlat.kFlat_of_flat`), whence so is `M̃^•`
  (`Stacks.TildeStalk.kFlatComplex_tilde`); this is the only place K-flatness is used, and it is
  what replaces `B ⊗ᴸ_A M^•` by the termwise base change `B ⊗_A M^•`;
* that degreewise pullback is `(B ⊗_A M^•)~` by Stacks 01I9 on complexes,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.tildePullbackComplexIso`, and
  `Stacks.Eta.DeterminantalIdeal.baseChangeCochainIso` identifies `B ⊗_A M^•` with the complex
  of the base-changed bounded complex.

The representative of `Lh^*M` on `Y` is produced by essential surjectivity of
`DerivedCategory.Q`; which representative it is does not matter, because restriction along an
open immersion is exact and therefore induces a functor on derived categories.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8S)
